    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic placement is otherwise excellent \u2014 the new `countOwnersRegisteredOn` sits naturally beside its siblings `countNamesakes`/`countOwnersInCity` and reuses their exact `findAll().stream().filter(...).count()` shape, the controller check mirrors the existing `CITY_CAPACITY` capacity-check idiom, and `DAILY_REGISTRATION_LIMIT` parallels `CITY_CAPACITY`. Nothing is duplicated and no class is becoming a catch-all.\n\nOne idiomatic inconsistency to fix:\n\n- **Fully-qualified `java.time.LocalDate` in the service layer breaks the codebase convention.** Both `ClinicService.java` (`countOwnersRegisteredOn(java.time.LocalDate date)`) and `ClinicServiceImpl.java:395` inline the fully-qualified type name. Every other file in this codebase that uses this type imports it and refers to it as `LocalDate` \u2014 `Owner.java`, `Pet.java`, `Visit.java` all do, and the controller in this very diff added `import java.time.LocalDate;` and uses the short name. A maintainer would find the FQN in the signature jarring. Add `import java.time.LocalDate;` to both service files and use `LocalDate date` in the interface method and impl to match.",
